        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-11 06:39:06.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten conf-sanity 103",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten conf-sanity 103\n\nconf-sanity test_103 renames the filesystem three times, each followed\nby a full stop and setupall: lustre to mylustre, to tfs, and back to\nlustre. The middle round only repeats the pool checks on a second\nname; the rename of an already renamed filesystem is still exercised\nby the rename back.\n\nDrop the tfs round and run the final pool checks after the rename back\nto the original name. Check the pool member added under mylustre and\nthe file created there after renaming back, so original-name logs\ncannot satisfy all checks. The filesystem is still left mounted for\nthe following tests. Destroy the test pools after the final checks so\nrepeated runs do not fail creating an existing pool. Refresh\ndevice-mapper aliases before renaming: mappings created in an earlier\nsubtest subshell are not inherited by later repetitions.\n\nOn a test VM, ONLY=103 took 100s, 107s, 100s and 95s before and 80s,\n66s and 70s after. CI averages 584s over 4433 runs per 30 days;\nremoving one of three rename rounds saves about 28% there, roughly\n160s per run, or about 200 hours per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=103\nAssisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.1-sol\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I13b4229b79c420de1adfcc6ade31d46e6c13129e\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70195\nReviewed-by: Alex Deiter <adeiter@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
